  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Vivos is transitioning from a legacy dentist-enrollment model toward an integrated medical-provider approach anchored by the acquisition of The Sleep Center of Nevada. This shift is fueling strong demand for in-center sleep testing and treatment services, while legacy VIP dentist and enrollment revenues are declining. The company is repositioning itself as a direct healthcare services provider in the large obstructive sleep apnea market, with sequential momentum building through 2025 as the new model scales.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is deliberately pivoting the business model to capture higher-value, recurring care pathways, but the transformation carries substantial operational strain. Operating expenses have surged, particularly in general and administrative costs, resulting in persistent cash burn despite revenue gains. A recent 19.9% stake taken by an outside investor group via a private placement signals external confidence and injects capital to fund the strategy, though near-term financial pressure remains a key test of execution.",
